  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday)\nIssued at 135 AM CDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nAs the upper low shifts east and northeast Tuesday, there will be a \nchance for some wrap-around showers across the north. Meanwhile, in \nthe wake of the severe weather a cold front will sweep across the \narea early Tuesday with strong, gusty northwest winds and cooler \ntemperatures. Highs Tuesday will again be in the 60s and lower 70s.\nMore tranquil weather is expected Wednesday as winds go light with \nmore sunshine. \n\nSome differences in the models as we go late in the week as Euro \nbrings a shortwave trough out of the central Rockies into the \nsouthern Plains Thursday with some low rain chances. Meanwhile, the \nGFS takes that shortwave east across the Dakotas. Otherwise, cool \nand quiet weather expected through the end of the week.",
